s, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions with clear error handling. Keep external behavior identical: same status codes, same response bodies. Need full refactored file. Need likely define sentinel errors: errInvalidID, errUserNotFound, errDatabase? But external behavior: 400 body {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no Content-Type? Original 400/404/500 do not set Content-Type. Success sets Content-Type application/json and encodes map. JSON encoder adds newline. Need preserve exact bodies? For success, json.Encoder.Encode(map[string]string{\"name\": name, \"email\": email}) produces {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\\n? Go map keys sorted alphabetically: email then name. Need preserve. If we use json.Marshal(map[string]string{...}) and write, no newline. That changes body. Need keep same response bodies. Could use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(user) for success. But if user struct with fields Name, Email", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0037130420096218586], [760, -6.715672969818115]], [[1144, -1.23978434203309e-05], [14235, -12.013516426086426]], [[4087, -0.011394199915230274], [310, -4.678765773773193]], [[1156, -0.03542401269078255], [303, -3.574192762374878]], [[579, -0.21313269436359406], [25, -2.4117982387542725]], [[1622, -0.0032498538494110107], [3296, -6.492381572723389]], [[13, -0.3368456959724426], [25, -1.6318743228912354]], [[14235, -0.03627682849764824], [1165, -4.068690299987793]], [[89109, -0.3403927683830261], [7936, -1.7838590145111084]], [[5805, -0.0002475687360856682], [2400, -8.691650390625]], [[9830, -0.025347372516989708], [6795, -3.7396132946014404]], [[6795, -2.837221290974412e-05], [17369, -11.92744255065918]], [[1083, -1.4016116857528687], [47781, -1.5741103887557983]], [[1228, -0.0949954241514206], [2400, -2.8037052154541016]], [[470, -3.194859891664237e-05], [5568, -10.640096664428711]], [[5568, -0.002913662465289235], [74243, -6.157898902893066]], [[440, -0.9170426726341248], [25, -1.868910789489746]], [[2708, -0.03587986156344414], [18101, -